  photo: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 0323463a6a48702488be66339a6a90a0, type: 3}
  title: "M\xE9kanik Destruktiw K\xF6mmand\xF6h \u2013 Early Zensor Concert, 1979"
  description: "One of the earliest known concert posters from Zensor, dated 3 November
    1979. Features the avant-garde Berlin group M\xE9kanik Destruktiw K\xF6mmand\xF6h
    alongside P/E, held at Belziger Str. 23."
  hasExtraInfo: 1
  extraInfoTitle: "M\xE9kanik Destruktiw K\xF6mmand\xF6h"
  extraInfoContent: "M\xE9kanik Destruktiw K\xF6mmand\xF6h (M.D.K.) was one of the
    most radical acts to emerge from the West Berlin underground in the late 1970s.
    Combining industrial noise, performance art, and political provocation, they
    embodied the chaotic energy of the city's divided, tension-filled environment.
    Their appearances at Zensor in 1979 were among the shop's very first live events,
    cementing Zensor's reputation as a space for music that existed outside any mainstream
    category."
  extraInfoImage: {fileID: 0}
